WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.501
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.701
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.133
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:08.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
I appreciate it.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.133
Guys,
some big entertainment news.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.934
Netflix has officially confirmed
that a second season

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.300
of "Squid Game" is coming soon.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.133
So, if you forgot what happened
in season one,

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.901
congrats --
that means therapy's working.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.834
Actually, after COVID, Ukraine,
and inflation,

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:28.968
critics are already calling it

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.434
"the feel-good comedy
of the year."

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:35.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.434
Yeah, this season's
gonna be pretty intense,

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.033
mostly 'cause all the players
are competing

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:45.000
for a single gallon of gas.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.834
Everyone's talking about this.
A senior software engineer

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.868
at Google was suspended
after he claimed

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.300
that the company's
artificial intelligence

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.634
has gotten so powerful,
it now functions like a person

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.300
with thoughts and feelings.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.167
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.467
Yeah, the engineer knew
the robot was a real person

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.567
when it forgot this weekend
is Father's Day.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:08.367
"Google last-minute
Father's Day gifts."

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.901
"You're a real boy!"

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.934
"Google grilling."

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.534
That's right.
The Google employee claims

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:26.434
the artificial intelligence
acts like a 7- or 8-year-old.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:29.000
Even more frightening,
here's what it looks like.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.901
Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.701
Well, some news from Washington.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:37.601
Today, Congress held the second
January 6th Committee hearing.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.267
Yep.
You know things are weird times

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.434
when the song of the summer
is the ABC News theme.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.934
[ "ABC News" theme plays ]

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:47.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.601
Uh, well, this morning on ABC,

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.734
they showed loud,
chaotic riot footage.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.734
And then, after that episode
of "The View" was over,

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.534
they showed the hearing.
And --

00:01:55.534 --> 00:02:00.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.634
You guys
are a good crowd tonight.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:02.734
I like this crowd.
-Yeah.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:05.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You guys get it

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:09.100
Stay with us all week!
I want this energy all week.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.701
I love this crowd.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.501
Fantastic.
That's right.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.968
So, today, every major network

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.367
covered the hearing,
even Fox News.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.167
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.300
They were like, "Might as well.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.634
All our anchors
are in it anyway."

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:25.868
So, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.567
Today's big witness
was supposed to be

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.667
Trump's former campaign manager,
Bill Stepien,

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.667
but he cancelled
at the last minute

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:36.167
because his wife
went into labor.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.200
When the baby was born,
the doctor was like,

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.601
"It's a...lucky break,
is what it is."

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:42.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:43.801
You know last night,
he was like,

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:46.100
"Honey, I made you a spicy
jalapeño casserole.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.234
Eat up.
Let's take the stairs.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.400
Let's take the stairs."

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.901
Listen to this.
For the first hearing,

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.801
on Thursday,
over 20 million people tuned in,

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.400
which is higher
than this year's NBA finals.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.167
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
Trump was torn.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.634
He didn't know whether
to worry about the hearing

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:07.067
or brag about the ratings.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.400
"Biggest riot ratings
in history.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.834
Just --"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.767
"Biggest.
People love the riot."

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:17.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
No, people don't love the --

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.601
Hey, I read that there's
a growing number of high-ranking

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:22.434
Democratic officials
who do not want President Biden

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.167
to run for re-election.

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.100
Biden believes that
he can get back on track

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.834
by crafting a tight,
concise message.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.033
And then he talked
for three hours

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.701
about how he plans to do that.

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.667
[ Laughter ]
Apparently --

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:37.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.901
-[ Clicks tongue ]

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.601
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.968
Foul ball.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:46.767
-Apparently, some Democrats
are worried about his age.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.767
Yeah. Bernie Sanders
is like, "I agree.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.434
He's too young!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:53.534
"He's too young,
these whippersnappers..."

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.100
"...wearing sneakers and..."

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.334
I saw that, due to a worldwide
shortage of helium --

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:05.000
this is true -- helium --
the National Weather Service

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.601
hasn't been able to launch
all their weather balloons.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.534
It's tough. And I think
I have a pretty good idea

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.067
of what the meetings inside

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.834
the National Weather Service
are like right now.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.200
-[ High-pitched voice ]
Dale, why don't we have

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.400
any weather balloons in the sky?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.501
-[ High-pitched voice ]
Well, Doug,

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:21.734
we don't have enough helium.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:24.100
And without it,
it's hard to get up real high.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.334
-I guess this is what happens
when there's inflation.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:29.067
-It's a real kick
in the weather balloons.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:32.000
[ Laughter ]
-Time to cut back on helium.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.801
[ Valve squeaks,
helium hissing stops ]

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:36.334
-[ Deep voice ]
What a sad day.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.601
-[ Deep voice ]
I know, Doug.

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:40.033
-Also, today's my birthday.
-Oh! Sorry.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.100
I almost forgot.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.968
Happy birthday.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.100
-Thanks!

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.434
-Doug, wait!

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.000
[ Explosion ]

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.267
-What?!
[ Laughing ]

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.968
-Yeah.
-Wait. What?

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.934
-Yeah.
-That happened?

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.868
-Yeah.
-They both had blonde hair.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.868
-Yeah, that's what I imagine
is happening.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.033
At the he-- at the National --

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:07.767
-And then helium
became a flammable substance.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.167
That's great.
That's beautiful.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:13.434
-Bill Nye over there.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:16.734
-And that guy had
a really deep voice naturally.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:17.834
-Yeah.
They both did, yeah.

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:19.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:20.534
Some business news, everybody.

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:22.133
Coca-Cola --
I'm kind of excited about this.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.367
Coca-Cola is teaming up
with Jack Daniel's

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:26.801
to release a Jack and Coke
cocktail in a can.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.434
[ Audience "Oohs," applauds ]
There it is.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:29.667
Look at that.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.367
-Finally, we no longer
have to go through that

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.767
exhausting task of mixing
Jack with Coke.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.000
Yep. Right now, there are
four cases of this stuff

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.467
holding up a rusted truck
in Kid Rock's front yard.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:45.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:48.267
Hey, get this. Yesterday,
15 McDonald's restaurants

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:50.534
in Russia reopened
with new branding

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:54.901
along with a new name,
called Vkusno &amp; Tochka,

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:57.434
which translates to
"Tasty and That's It."

00:05:57.434 --> 00:06:00.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:02.901
"Tasty and that's it."
-No more.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.701
-Yep, they're really trying
to distance themselves

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.501
from the existing
McDonald's brand.

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:08.834
Check out this ad --
this latest ad I saw.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.701
-[ Russian accent ]
If you're a fan of McDonald's,

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:13.968
then you'll love, or at least
tolerate, Vkusno &amp; Tochka.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.534
We offer all of menu favorite,

00:06:15.534 --> 00:06:18.968
including fraction-of-kilogram
burger with dairy square,

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.100
room-temperature
potato shavings,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.934
deep-fried poultry blocks,

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.234
the crispy traitor --

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:25.868
we mean chicken sandwich,

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:27.501
and milk sludge.

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:29.601
And if you see missing clown,
Donald McRonald,

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.367
please report to authorities.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:32.934
Vkusno &amp; Tochka.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.467
♪ Ba-da, ba-ba-ba ♪

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.133
You will loving it.

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:37.834
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:40.968
-"You will loving it."

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:44.267
To distance themselves.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:45.467
Hey, did you guys
hear about this?

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:48.000
Marvel has announced that
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.501
is going to return to theaters
with new and extended scenes.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:55.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:57.567
Do people really
care about that?

00:06:57.567 --> 00:06:58.968
[ Audience shouting "Yeah" ]

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.133
-Really? I thought it was like,
"See it again

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:03.000
but now with the scenes
that weren't good enough

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.067
for the real movie."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.067 --> 00:07:06.868
Speaking of Spider-Man,
over at Disneyland,

00:07:06.868 --> 00:07:08.767
they have a Spider-Man show,
right?

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:10.434
And there's a dummy
that's supposed to do

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:12.534
flips in the air and land on top
of a building

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:14.801
like it's Spider-Man,
but something went wrong.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.634
And someone got video of it.
Watch this.

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:18.067
-Here goes something.

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:19.634
♪♪

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.300
-There he goes.
You're the man, Spidey.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.534
Good luck, Spidey.

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:24.434
Good luck -- ooh!

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:27.634
[ Laughter ]
[ Wah-wah! ]

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:31.634
Ooh!
[ Laughter continues ]

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:34.100
Looks like Spider-Man after
a six pack of Jack and Coke.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.167
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:37.801
"Hey, buddy!"

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:39.334
That's actually
in the extended scene

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:43.467
from the new "Spider-Man" movie
in theaters and IMAX.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:48.767
And IMAX, of course.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.234
Guys, some entertainment news.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:52.300
A lot of fans are theorizing
that Beyoncé

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.000
has a new album coming soon
because of mysterious clues

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.734
that she dropped online
this weekend.

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.868
-Yeah, but how do you know
for sure?

00:07:59.868 --> 00:08:01.200
Isn't that just a rumor?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.100
-I mean, the clues
are everywhere, Tariq.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.000
-Like what?
-Okay.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.234
So, on Friday, Beyoncé
deleted her profile pictures

00:08:08.234 --> 00:08:09.734
for all her social-media
accounts --

00:08:09.734 --> 00:08:11.200
Twitter, Instagram, TikTok,
all of them.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.234
And she still hasn't uploaded
new ones over 72 hours later.

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:15.968
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:08:15.968 --> 00:08:17.334
-Go on.

00:08:17.334 --> 00:08:19.901
-Beyoncé's most recent studio
album was "Lemonade,"

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:22.667
which was surprise released
over six years ago in 2016.

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:24.400
But you know
what else happened in 2016?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.601
Her second Super Bowl
performance,

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:27.033
the one with Coldplay.

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:28.834
And we all know what happened
the day before that performance.

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:31.334
She surprise released the song
for the video "Formation."

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:32.868
Then immediately after
the Super Bowl, the next day,

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:34.868
she announced The Formation
World Tour all before

00:08:34.868 --> 00:08:36.667
anyone even knew that she was
going to surprise release

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:38.234
"Lemonade" that April!

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:40.968
-Well, that was 2016, though.

00:08:40.968 --> 00:08:42.767
-Right, right, right,
but both "Lemonade"

00:08:42.767 --> 00:08:44.968
and her self-titled
surprise album, "Beyoncé,"

00:08:44.968 --> 00:08:46.801
had sneaky clues
before their release, too,

00:08:46.801 --> 00:08:49.367
like Beyoncé posting pictures
of herself with lemons.

00:08:49.367 --> 00:08:51.400
And on Saturday, fans realized

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.567
that if you search
Saturday's date, June 11th,

00:08:53.567 --> 00:08:55.767
on Beyoncé website,
placeholder art

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:57.234
for a mysterious Beyoncé album

00:08:57.234 --> 00:08:59.167
that's just called "B7" came up.

00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:02.334
"B7." Beyoncé's seventh album.
Get it?

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:04.934
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:07.067
-But she didn't release an album
this weekend.

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:08.934
-Are you even listening?
'Cause then Tidal,

00:09:08.934 --> 00:09:11.767
the streaming service that Jay-Z
is on the board of,

00:09:11.767 --> 00:09:13.801
tweeted, "What is a B7?"

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:17.400
Then just "B8."
Jay-Z is Beyoncé's husband.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:22.634
So, if and when Beyoncé
puts out a new album,

00:09:22.634 --> 00:09:24.734
it could be "B7" and "B8."

00:09:24.734 --> 00:09:27.334
That's a double album.
Isn't that crazy?!

00:09:27.334 --> 00:09:30.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.734
-Oh, it's crazy all right.

00:09:32.734 --> 00:09:34.701
Crazy in love!

00:09:34.701 --> 00:09:36.734
[ Roots play "Crazy in Love" ]

00:09:36.734 --> 00:09:38.868
♪♪

00:09:38.868 --> 00:09:40.300
-All right.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:47.400
Moving on.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.267
I heard that some companies

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:52.167
are allowing workers
to wear shorts --

00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.200
-Wait!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.868
[ Roots play "Crazy in Love" ]

00:09:59.868 --> 00:10:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:03.934
You're not gonna crawl
on all fours?

00:10:03.934 --> 00:10:06.133
-When it comes on, I've got to
get in my -- my moves, man.

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:09.934
Guys, moving on.
I heard that, uh...

00:10:09.934 --> 00:10:11.968
[ Laughter ]

00:10:11.968 --> 00:10:14.767
...some companies are allowing
workers to wear shorts

00:10:14.767 --> 00:10:17.701
in an effort to get them back
in the office this summer.

00:10:17.701 --> 00:10:19.734
Yeah. You know a CEO
is desperate when they're like,

00:10:19.734 --> 00:10:21.567
"Fine.
You don't have to wear pants."

00:10:21.567 --> 00:10:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:23.234 --> 00:10:25.133
